# Day 10 Notes

## Process Synchronization

Process Synchronization ensures proper execution when multiple processes access shared resources.

---

## Race Condition

Occurs when multiple threads modify shared data simultaneously.

Result:
- Data Inconsistency
- Incorrect Output

---

## Critical Section

Part of the program where shared resources are accessed.

Example:
count++;

---

## Requirements

### Mutual Exclusion
Only one process can enter the critical section.

### Progress
No unnecessary waiting.

### Bounded Waiting
Every process eventually gets a chance.

---

